Pros:
++ Extremely satisfying melee combat (each weapon feels unique);
++ High Replayability (skaven threats are unleashed every time differently)
+ Interesting Loot & Crafting  System (weapon traits make sense)
+ No microtransactions (seriously!);
+ Fun & original missions;
+ Rich Warhammer Lore;
+ Witty voiceovers + story narration (sometimes they way player characters react to surrounding reminds of Dragon Age/Mass Effect games);
+ dev team is quick to react to whatever issues;

A few things that give this game alot of potential as a open world sandbox game is;
But  what I dislike about the game;
Aside from building stuff and killing creatures, there just isn't enough motivation or purpose to playing the game.  It needs more players on the multiplayer servers as well. I will review this game in another month or two and update my review.

Well, this is an OK game. 6.5/10. It has potential but some small details made it a medium-quality game.
Pros:
- Nice story;
- Nice graphics;
- Involving story-line;
- Interesting puzzles;
Cons:
- Stupid controls - you are forced to commit mistakes over and over again;
- Terrible animations - melee and death animation could have been improved;
- Parkour guy can't swimg (?);
- Too short (5.9 hours);
This is the kind of game you should buy only if it is on sale (less than 5 bucks). I don't think I would pay much for it, considering I got really♥♥♥♥♥♥♥♥in 90% of my deaths. Some ocasions I was forced to commit a lot of movement mistakes due to its stupid non-quick system control.
If you like pos-apocalypse games you should buy it to have a bit of fun. Also its platform helps making a bit of a change from the FPS we have out there.

Well I have been turned away from playing this game much since Squad 2.0 was added, as it has kept me from playing the game the way the meta was sold to me.   This game is only driving me further away with each new feature added. Spawn Token 1.0 is the nail in the proverbial coffin for me, I am moving my time, funding and energies into helping Hell Let Loose be the best WW2 FPS.
